<task id="037" project="customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Wire Cosmos client for L2 — partition /customerId, partition-key predicate on every read/write (§4D I3)</title>
    <phase>C Wave C3 — L2 Control-Plane Scaffold</phase>
    <gate>blocked</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Auth-adjacent (UAMI Cosmos data-plane RBAC per task 030) + l2-controlplane tag + enforces §4D I3 tenant-isolation invariant. task-create Step 3.5.5 FULL (l2-controlplane; NEW surface; downstream reconciler + all 19 handlers depend).</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Brief rubric: L2 scaffold + reconciler tier. Getting the Cosmos client shape right (UAMI credential + partition-key discipline + optimistic concurrency for I5) is architectural — the whole state store hinges on this wiring. "Opus 4.8 / Fable 5 for L2 scaffold + UAMI migration + reconciler".</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>waveC3-parallel</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Deps on task 024 (POCO shape) and task 036 (project scaffold + DI + Program.cs). Also touches Program.cs which is shared with tasks 038/039 — sequential to avoid merge conflict.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>024, 036</deps>
    <tags>l2-controlplane, azure, auth, api, cache</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-6 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Wire the Cosmos client into src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/ via a new CosmosModule.cs: register CosmosClient (Azure.Cosmos SDK) using DefaultAzureCredential (which resolves to the L2 App Service's bound UAMI at runtime — task 028/029/030) OR ManagedIdentityCredential with explicit clientId; register an IProvisioningRunRepository abstraction that (a) enforces partition key = /customerId on every ReadItemAsync / CreateItemAsync / ReplaceItemAsync per §4D I3, (b) uses ETag-based optimistic concurrency for the same-customer-serialization guard per FR-23 I5. Reference the existing BFF Cosmos client patterns as canonical (read-only reference; do NOT compile-depend).</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer with Azure.Cosmos SDK + Managed Identity credential expertise. Understand §4D I3: every Cosmos operation MUST include partition-key predicate; ArchTest (Wave C6) will fail the build if a call lacks it. Understand FR-23 I5: same-customer runs serialized via optimistic concurrency (409 on conflict with winning run ID).</role>
  <goal>src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Modules/CosmosModule.cs + Repositories/IProvisioningRunRepository.cs + Repositories/CosmosProvisioningRunRepository.cs exist; CosmosClient is registered in DI with UAMI credential; the repository interface exposes ReadRunAsync(customerId, runId), CreateRunAsync(run), ReplaceRunAsync(run, etag), each requiring PartitionKey(customerId); dotnet build passes; a smoke test against a dev Cosmos account verifies CRUD round-trip.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-27 + FR-30 (§4D I3) + FR-23 (I5 concurrency): the L2 control plane reads/writes ProvisioningRun documents in the spaarke-provisioning/runs container (task 024). Partition key /customerId; every read/write MUST include the partition-key predicate — no cross-partition queries. Same-customer runs serialize via optimistic concurrency on sprk_currentrunid (Dataverse side, task 023) AND on the ProvisioningRun document ETag (Cosmos side, this task). Without this wiring, no handler can persist state; no reconciler can advance the DAG.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Modules/CosmosModule.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Repositories/IProvisioningRunRepository.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Repositories/CosmosProvisioningRunRepository.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Program.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/ (BFF Cosmos client patterns — read for reference, do NOT compile-depend)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Models/ProvisioningRun.cs (task 024)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">infrastructure/bicep/modules/uami.bicep (task 028)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="024" status="pending">ProvisioningRun POCO + database/container schema — the type shape this repository persists.</dependency>
      <dependency task="036" status="pending">L2 project scaffold + Program.cs + module composition pattern.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Scope: Cosmos client MUST use UAMI credential (DefaultAzureCredential resolves to bound UAMI in-App-Service; ManagedIdentityCredential with explicit clientId is the more explicit variant). Do NOT use account-key credential — task 030 grants Cosmos DB Built-in Data Contributor to UAMI principal.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-036">Scope: reuse existing BFF Cosmos client PATTERNS (naming, exception handling, retry policy) via canonical reference reading; do NOT reference Sprk.Bff.Api assemblies.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">§4D I3 acceptance: EVERY ReadItemAsync / CreateItemAsync / ReplaceItemAsync / UpsertItemAsync / DeleteItemAsync call MUST include explicit PartitionKey. Task 025 ArchTest (or a paired I3 ArchTest in Wave C6) will fail the build if a call lacks it — write compliant code from day 1.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">FR-23 I5 acceptance: same-customer serialization uses optimistic concurrency. ReplaceRunAsync signature MUST accept ETag; on ETagPreconditionFailedException the repo returns a typed 409 result NOT an exception — the endpoint layer maps this to HTTP 409 with the winning runId.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope (this task only): Cosmos client + repository interface + implementation. Do NOT wire Service Bus (task 038) or App Insights (task 039). Do NOT implement any handler; do NOT implement the state-reconciler (Wave C5).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">MUST enable Cosmos client-level telemetry via ITelemetryClient (App Insights wiring in task 039 will pick this up); do NOT log secrets or full parameter dumps (KV URI refs OK; scan for cleartext-secret patterns per task 025 ArchTest).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Publish-size impact reported per L2's own baseline (not BFF NFR-01).</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Azure.Cosmos SDK; UAMI credential; partition-key discipline; optimistic concurrency</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/design.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/CLAUDE.md</file>
