      <file>.claude/constraints/data.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/auth.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/caching/</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Existing BFF Cosmos client wiring" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/">Read for reference — mirror the client construction, retry policy, exception handling; do NOT compile-depend.</pattern>
      <pattern name="Optimistic concurrency (ETag)" location="Azure.Cosmos SDK docs">Use ItemRequestOptions.IfMatchEtag on ReplaceItemAsync; catch CosmosException with StatusCode == PreconditionFailed.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="prescriptive">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Output the RIGOR LEVEL declaration (FULL + reason — l2-controlplane + auth + §4D I3 enforcement). Load spec.md FR-27 + FR-30 + FR-23, ADR-028, ADR-036, task 024 POCO shape.</step>
    <step order="1">Add PackageReference for Microsoft.Azure.Cosmos (latest stable — verify zero HIGH CVE) + Azure.Identity to Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.csproj.</step>
    <step order="2">Author Modules/CosmosModule.cs: extension method AddCosmosModule(this IServiceCollection services) registering CosmosClient singleton using DefaultAzureCredential (bound to UAMI at runtime) with the account endpoint from IConfiguration.</step>
    <step order="3">Author Repositories/IProvisioningRunRepository.cs with methods ReadRunAsync(string customerId, string runId, CancellationToken), CreateRunAsync(ProvisioningRun run, CancellationToken), ReplaceRunAsync(ProvisioningRun run, string ifMatchEtag, CancellationToken) returning a typed Result&lt;ProvisioningRun, ConcurrencyConflict&gt;.</step>
    <step order="4">Author Repositories/CosmosProvisioningRunRepository.cs implementing the interface — every call passes new PartitionKey(customerId); ReplaceRunAsync catches CosmosException StatusCode == PreconditionFailed and returns ConcurrencyConflict with the current stored run's ID (I5).</step>
    <step order="5">Register the repository + Cosmos module in Program.cs (extending task 036's composition).</step>
    <step order="6">Author a smoke test at src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Tests/CosmosSmokeTests.cs (create the Tests project if not present) that hits a dev Cosmos account (skipped by default under an env-guard) verifying CRUD round-trip.</step>
    <step order="7">Run dotnet build src/server/services/ — verify 0 errors, 0 warnings.</step>
    <step order="8">Run dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive — verify 0 HIGH CVEs.</step>
    <step order="9">Update TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="10">Document deviation (e.g. DefaultAzureCredential vs explicit ManagedIdentityCredential, retry policy nuance) in projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If DI registration for CosmosClient collides with the BFF's Cosmos client registration in a shared assembly OR causes a captive-dependency graph error, STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6 — L2 must own its own Cosmos client lifecycle.</trigger>
    <trigger>If Microsoft.Azure.Cosmos has a HIGH-severity CVE at the version chosen, STOP and escalate — do NOT introduce a package with an open HIGH per NFR-02.</trigger>
    <trigger>If §4D I3 partition-key discipline cannot be enforced at the repository interface level (e.g. Cosmos SDK forces a code path without partition key), STOP and escalate — the ArchTest wave (C6) will fail the build otherwise.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane/Modules/CosmosModule.cs</output>
