  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given dotnet build, 0 errors + 0 warnings.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a code inspection of CosmosProvisioningRunRepository.cs, every Cosmos SDK call (Read/Create/Replace/Upsert/Delete) includes an explicit new PartitionKey(customerId) — §4D I3 compliant.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a ReplaceRunAsync call with a stale etag, the repository returns Result.ConcurrencyConflict with the current stored runId — NOT an exception (I5 serialization signal).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a smoke test against dev Cosmos, CRUD round-trip succeeds and reads return the same ProvisioningRun document.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no account-key credential used; Azure.Identity DefaultAzureCredential (which resolves to UAMI at runtime) is the ONLY credential path.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no Service Bus or App Insights wiring in this task.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive, 0 HIGH CVEs.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Maps spec.md FR-27 + FR-30 (§4D I3) + FR-23 (I5). The typed ConcurrencyConflict return signal is what enables Wave C5's endpoint layer to return HTTP 409 with the winning runId (per FR-23 acceptance). Coordinate with task 025 (ArchTest) — a paired I3 ArchTest may be authored in Wave C6 that verifies partition-key discipline; write this code to pass such an ArchTest by construction.</notes>

